<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 23 June, from 1314 to 2016.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bannockburn" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bannockburn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1314 CE <span class="tih-ago">712 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Bannockburn begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the first day, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a> killed the English knight Henry de Bohun in single combat before the armies. Edward II's larger army was routed the next day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1757 CE <span class="tih-ago">269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Clive defeats the Nawab of Bengal at Plassey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Helped by the defection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-jafar">Mir Jafar</a>, Clive's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> troops defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraj-ud-daulah">Siraj ud-Daulah</a>. The victory gave the Company control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and launched British territorial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1848 CE <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">June Days uprising erupts in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Workers rose after the government closed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-workshops">National Workshops</a>. General Cavaignac crushed them in four days; thousands were killed and many more deported.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1868 CE <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Latham Sholes patents a typewriter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sholes and his partners received a patent for a 'Type-Writer'. Developed further and sold by Remington, it popularised the QWERTY keyboard and transformed office work.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1972 CE <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nixon approves using the CIA to block the Watergate inquiry</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a taped conversation, Nixon agreed that the CIA should ask the FBI to halt its investigation. The release of this 'smoking gun' tape in August 1974 forced his resignation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2016 CE <span class="tih-ago">10 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United Kingdom votes to leave the European Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a referendum, 52 per cent voted to leave the EU. Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Cameron resigned, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> formally left in January 2020.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
